Thought:[32;1m[1;3mFinal Answer:

#### Sets and Indices

Let $I$ be the set of vehicle types (indexed by $i$), with ProductName as identifier.

#### Parameters

- $p_i$: Profit from selling one unit of vehicle type $i$ (Value column).
- $w_i$: Weight (stock space required) for one unit of vehicle type $i$ (Weight column).
- $C$: Total inventory capacity (Capacity column from capacity.csv).

#### Decision Variables

- $x_i$: Number of vehicles of type $i$ to order per day. ($x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0}$)

#### Objective

Maximize total profit:
$$
\max \sum_{i \in I} p_i x_i
$$

#### Constraint

Total stock space used cannot exceed capacity:
$$
\sum_{i \in I} w_i x_i \leq C
$$

#### Variable Domains

$$
x_i \in \mathbb{Z}_{\geq 0} \quad \forall i \in I
$$

